SmartCare v0.1 – Initial Engineering Brief and AI Activity Card

Part A — Understand the Problem

What data must be stored in the system?
•	Patient name
•	Practitioner name
•	Appointment time
•	Practitioner schedule 

What functions might be useful?
•	book_appointment() — to command a new appointment for the patient.
•	display_appointments() — to display all the recorded information of the appointments of the patients.
•	A function to keep a check whether required information has been entered.
What could go wrong?
•	Incorrect patient’s record
•	Incorrect practitioner’s Record
•	Missing appointment time of the patients
•	collaboration of the two patients time at same time from the same practitioner 
•	Improper format of keeping record of the patient 

What requirements are unclear?
•	Whether the patient can book their appointment themselves online 
•	Whether appointments need to be saved permanently in the memory or for the temporary time.
•	Whom should be permitted the access to the information 

Part B — Human Written Prototype

five limitations
1.	Appointments are not saved permanently.  Appointments are not sotred in the memory permanently, they disappear when the program closes.
2.	There is no proper management for keeping the data or the record of the patient’s information 
3.	There is no proper management of the appointments time and a program to keep check the schedule and the appointments of the patients are properly matched or not 
4.	There is no proper format set up for the Patients required to book an appointment 
5.	There is no Login system in the software so the patient cannot keep the track of their appointment details properly 
6.	There is not provided the proper feature in the system to edit the appointment 



